# Clean Code (bonus 10)

- Small focused modules; one responsibility per use-case/adapter/component.
- Meaningful names; no provider brand in identifiers.
- No business logic in HTTP handlers — Hexagonal layers stay strict.
- Prefer early returns / ROP over deep nesting; avoid dead code and commented-out blocks.
- Consistent formatting (Prettier/ESLint); shared types in `packages/shared` instead of duplicated DTOs.
- Errors: typed domain errors → mapped HTTP; no swallowed catches.
- Keep PRs/commits incremental and reviewable (anti-fraud: visible progress history).
